    "title": "Writing Essays 3: a compare and contrast essay",
    "paragraphs": [
        {
            "structure": {
                "para": [
                    {
                        "id": "2",
                        "text": "Writing Essays 3: a compare and contrast essay"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "3",
                        "text": "The compare and contrast essay is used when you need to point out similarities (compare) or differences (contrast) between two or more theories, arguments or ideas."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "notes": {
                "para": []
            },
            "content": {
                "para": [],
                "placeHolder": "",
                "id": ""
            }
        },
        {
            "structure": {
                "para": [
                    {
                        "id": "5",
                        "text": "Title"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "6",
                        "text": "The title of the essay or the question that the essay answers"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "7",
                        "text": "TIP If you are asked to write a critique, in addition to showing your understanding of the similarities and differences between the issues, you will need to display an element of critical evaluation. This means you need to question the information you read and assess its validity.",
                        "tip": true
                    }
                ]
            },
            "notes": {
                "para": []
            },
            "content": {
                "para": [
                    [
                        {
                            "id": "8",
                            "text": " Examine any two development theories, evaluating their effectiveness. "
                        }
                    ]
                ],
                "placeHolder": "Type your Title here.",
                "id": "8"
            }
        },
        {
            "structure": {
                "para": [
                    {
                        "id": "10",
                        "text": "Paragraph 1: Introduction"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "11",
                        "text": "Begin with a general statement on the topic.\nClearly state the theories, arguments or ideas to be compared.\nState the aims and organization of the essay."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "notes": {
                "para": []
            },
            "content": {
                "para": [
                    [
                        {
                            "id": "13",
                            "text": " The concept of development "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "12",
                            "text": " as a means to alleviate poverty and improve the lives of people "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "82",
                            "text": " is an extremely complex, problematic thesis "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "12",
                            "text": " ... "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "14",
                            "text": " This essay will focus on two development theories: firstly "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "12",
                            "text": " , Rostow's 1960 … modernization theory, "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "83",
                            "text": " and secondly "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "12",
                            "text": " dependency theory. "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "15",
                            "text": " Both of these theories will be examined critically "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "12",
                            "text": " by placing them in a wider temporal context, "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "84",
                            "text": " and their effectiveness evaluated "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "12",
                            "text": " in relation to their practical application. "
                        }
                    ]
                ],
                "placeHolder": "Type your Introduction here.",
                "id": "12"
            }
        },
        {
            "structure": {
                "para": [
                    {
                        "id": "17",
                        "text": "Paragraph 2"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "18",
                        "text": "A description and explanation of the first theory, argument or idea"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "19",
                        "text": "TIP Use research and provide supporting evidence.",
                        "tip": true
                    }
                ]
            },
            "notes": {
                "para": []
            },
            "content": {
                "para": [
                    [
                        {
                            "id": "20",
                            "text": " Modernization theory is a concept explicated … by American economist Walt Rostow in 1960. Rostow outlines five stages … [Description of the five stages follows (omitted here).] … This conceptualization of development can therefore be seen to offer an optimistic pathway for countries to follow and ultimately achieve modernization. "
                        }
                    ]
                ],
                "placeHolder": "Type Paragraph 2 here.",
                "id": "20"
            }
        },
        {
            "structure": {
                "para": [
                    {
                        "id": "24",
                        "text": "Paragraph 3"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "25",
                        "text": "Evaluation of the first theory, argument or idea"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "notes": {
                "para": []
            },
            "content": {
                "para": [
                    [
                        {
                            "id": "26",
                            "text": " The thematic, structured approach by Rostow presents value for examination … [Evaluation of the theory follows (omitted here).] ... Three further fundamental problems undermine Rostow's model … [Three problems are stated (omitted here).] These criticisms are echoed by Kothari and Minogue (2002) … It is clear that there are a variety of limitations … "
                        }
                    ]
                ],
                "placeHolder": "Type Paragraph 3 here.",
                "id": "26"
            }
        },
        {
            "structure": {
                "para": []
            },
            "notes": {
                "para": []
            },
            "content": {
                "para": [
                    [
                        {
                            "id": "28",
                            "text": " The thematic, structured approach by Rostow presents value for examination … [Evaluation of the theory follows (omitted here).] ... Three further fundamental problems "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "29",
                            "text": " undermine "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "28",
                            "text": " Rostow's model … [Three problems are stated (omitted here).] These criticisms are echoed by Kothari and Minogue (2002) … "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "30",
                            "text": " It is clear that "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "28",
                            "text": " there are a variety of "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "31",
                            "text": " limitations "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "28",
                            "text": " … "
                        }
                    ]
                ],
                "placeHolder": "Type Paragraph 3 here.",
                "id": "28",
                "duplicate": true
