            "content": {
                "para": [
                    [
                        {
                            "id": "72",
                            "text": " In conclusion, it is clear that "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "73",
                            "text": " both Rostow's modernization model and dependency theory have attempted to address the complex notion of development in different ways. … "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "86",
                            "text": " The two theories, however, have received extensive criticism … "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "74",
                            "text": " The overall contribution of modernization theory and dependency theory cannot be entirely disregarded "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "72",
                            "text": " , as they have each helped contemporary development theories realize their present form, "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "75",
                            "text": " but their effectiveness in their own right holds little practical value within the current field of development. "
                        }
                    ]
                ],
